  "goodToKnow": "Angrenzend means adjacent or neighbouring: das angrenzende Zimmer, die angrenzenden Gemeinden. It's the present participle of angrenzen an (to border on): Deutschland grenzt an neun Länder, more than any other European country. Die Grenze (border) came into German from Slavic languages around the 13th century and replaced the old native word Mark. Synonyms: benachbart, nebenan."
